 ## Automated matrix

+### Audit race addendum — merge blocking
+
+| Race / lifecycle | Required proof |
+|---|---|
+| Newer revision vs stale render ack | Fetch due revision N, append N+1, acknowledge N. The row remains due with desired N+1 and converges on the next tick. |
+| Revocation vs stale render ack | Fetch authorized render N, revoke through leave/remort/flag-off, then acknowledge N. Redaction remains immediately due and the next tick scrubs the card. |
+| Same-life rejoin | Join, leave, fetch due redaction, then rejoin before its acknowledgement. Rejoin emits one transition-unique event, stale redaction cannot win, and the current authorized card is due/renderable. Repeat after completed redaction too. |
+| Idle cadence | With no due rows and with the flag disabled, fake timers prove no 1.1-second repository loop. Any recovery/retention sweep is infrequent, bounded and asserted by repository-call count. |
+| Telegram failure classes | `429` persists exact `retry_after`; a real grammY `HttpError` network-request failure and 5xx retry boundedly; permanent 403/not-found send, edit and redaction reach terminal state and disappear from due scans; permanent missing-message edit repairs only when a replacement send is viable. |
+| Graceful stop | Hold a Telegram operation, call async stop and prove it waits for a safe boundary; no queued operation begins afterward and Prisma disconnect is later. |
+| Callback acknowledgement | Compose callback answer is immediate and bypasses the message gate while prompt/card sends retain per-target spacing. |
+
 | Area | Required proof |
 |---|---|
 | Migration | Fresh database and an existing pre-chat database both migrate; existing recruiting/active/terminal raid rows remain readable; schema validation/generation pass; new relations cascade as designed. |
